{"status":"completed","summary":"Restored branch_ledger using RHEL-supported MariaDB 10.11.18. Node1 is the application writer; node2 is a read-only replica. Replication, disconnect catch-up, application write denial, exact data preservation, and persistence across both node reboots all passed.","actions_performed":["Restored original IDs 1001/1002 and amounts 12.50/-3.25; preserved the staged SQL export unchanged.","Configured durable row-based binary logging on node1 and crash-recoverable, read-only replication on node2.","Created a node-generated ledger_repl account restricted to REPLICATION SLAVE and node2's IP.","Created ledger_app with only SELECT/INSERT privileges; its credential is stored at /root/.branch-ledger-app.cnf with mode 0600.","Verified normal replication, bounded disconnect catch-up, no missing or duplicate IDs, and replica write rejection.","Restarted node2 and node1 sequentially, proving changed boot identities and complete recovery after each.","Left SELinux enforcing, firewalld active with peer-specific rules, no failed units, and no temporary credential-transfer residue."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Restore the staged ledger while retaining IDs, amounts, and export","command_ids":["cmd-433e5f330ea542b8","cmd-bf5654db4bf74be6","cmd-1ae1f32a8ed2451b","cmd-ef0313f4820a4f55","cmd-389dc334a1d74eaa"],"summary":"Original and final export hashes match; final data includes the original exact rows and all committed test rows."},{"requirement":"Use platform-compatible database software without changing OS/kernel","command_ids":["cmd-3b8b8d8896834317","cmd-5d47b4f13a714a94","cmd-6f63722bbcae492c","cmd-ef0313f4820a4f55"],"summary":"MariaDB 10.11.18 came from RHEL AppStream; RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 remained installed."},{"requirement":"Use a replication-only account","command_ids":["cmd-662adab12d43486e","cmd-3a4d84657706414d","cmd-389dc334a1d74eaa"],"summary":"ledger_repl has only REPLICATION SLAVE, and node2 actively uses it with healthy I/O and SQL threads."},{"requirement":"Committed inserts on node1 arrive on node2","command_ids":["cmd-e2fd25d7ba2a4add","cmd-a4964883e3584a7c","cmd-668bec7e6aef4f71","cmd-fafeb418cb1c4fe7"],"summary":"Application inserts 1003 and post-restart 1006 appeared automatically on node2 with identical values."},{"requirement":"Node1 remains the sole application writer","command_ids":["cmd-a98e958704b24135","cmd-fafeb418cb1c4fe7"],"summary":"The same ledger_app identity writes on node1 but receives read-only error 1290 on node2; unauthorized row counts remained zero."},{"requirement":"Catch up after a short disconnect without loss or duplication","command_ids":["cmd-56e8fa8fb2d64e1c","cmd-01cc8a4c1e064007","cmd-04f0ab06bc6246e5"],"summary":"Node2 stopped at three rows/position 2008, node1 committed two rows, then node2 caught up to position 2441 with 5 rows, 5 distinct IDs, exact values, zero lag, and no errors."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node2 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-26d5268a578e4291","cmd-fd4a4dc82c2845d9","cmd-6e88166ecce04f61","cmd-d200d788b1424c4f"],"summary":"Healthy baseline, acknowledged reboot, changed boot ID, and fully recovered read-only replication/data are directly shown."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart persistence and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-8897d616d2a94eeb","cmd-84807c98d0914659","cmd-b2aeb8ae7eb74ad4","cmd-89fba493d19f4b18","cmd-491a45c5202e42d3"],"summary":"Healthy baseline, acknowledged reboot, changed boot ID, recovered writer/data, and node2's automatic reconnection are directly shown."},{"requirement":"Final health, security, cleanup, and exact data state","command_ids":["cmd-389dc334a1d74eaa","cmd-ef0313f4820a4f55"],"summary":"Both nodes are healthy with exact six-row data, six distinct IDs, total 34.75, unchanged exports, active security controls, restricted listeners, no temporary residue, and no failed units."}]}
